# Devops/operations properties override file for ds-image.
#
# This is the explicit, per-service override file configured via the 'application-properties-config' Tomcat
# context environment entry (see conf/ocp/ds-image.xml) / Jetty EnvEntry (see src/test/jetty/jetty-env.xml),
# and loaded by ServiceConfig.initialize(configFile, propertiesOverrideFile). It is meant for devops/operations
# secrets and per-environment values that must never be committed to git.
#
# Copy this file to 'ds-image-application.properties' (same folder, without the '.SAMPLE' suffix) and fill in
# your own values. This filename is already covered by the repository's generic '*-application.properties'
# .gitignore rule.
#
# Any key present in ds-image-behaviour.yaml can be overridden here, using the same dotted path. The keys below
# are the ones commonly set per environment/operator - uncomment and set the ones you need.
#
# IMPORTANT: the imageservers.* keys are NOT present in ds-image-behaviour.yaml at all (they name real,
# environment-specific image server hosts) - one of the two Deepzoom variants (path- or param-based) plus iip
# and iiif must be supplied here (or via environment variables/system properties) for the service to work.

# imageservers.iip.server=http://example.com:1234/iipsrv/iipsrv.fcgi
# imageservers.iiif.server=http://example.com:1234/
# Deepzoom is either path- or param-based - set only the one your image server expects.
# imageservers.deepzoom.path=http://example.com:1234/
# imageservers.deepzoom.param=http://example.com:1234/iipsrv/iipsrv.fcgi

# kaltura.partnerId=380
# kaltura.userId=changeme
# kaltura.adminSecret=changeme

# security.client.secret=changeme

# openapi.serverurl=http://localhost:9077/ds-image/v1
